usage: run_pit.py [-h]
                  --subject {commons-lang,flink,hibernate,jgrapht,petclinic,quarkus,spring-core,spring-security}
                  [--class TARGET] --checkout CHECKOUT [--output OUTPUT]
                  [--mvn MVN] [--cpus CPUS] [--plan]
                  [--job-timeout JOB_TIMEOUT] [--gradle-arg GRADLE_ARG]

Replay the recorded PIT scope on a user-provided checkout; never checks out
code.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --subject {commons-lang,flink,hibernate,jgrapht,petclinic,quarkus,spring-core,spring-security}
  --class TARGET
  --checkout CHECKOUT
  --output OUTPUT
  --mvn MVN
  --cpus CPUS
  --plan                Print configuration and commands without launching a
                        build or PIT
  --job-timeout JOB_TIMEOUT
                        Gradle replay wall-clock timeout in seconds, including
                        build; 0 disables it (not a PIT mutation timeout)
  --gradle-arg GRADLE_ARG
                        Additional Gradle build argument; use --gradle-
                        arg=VALUE, repeatable; record every override
